 ### [Axis-Aligned Plane Intersection](12131-axis-aligned-plane-intersection.md)
-Intersects a ray with an axis-aligned plane defined by an anchor point, extent, and direction index `d`. It returns the intersection distance `t` and barycentric-like coordinates `u, v`. The method uses a direction index to permute coordinate axes, aligning the plane normal with a single axis to simplify the intersection calculation.
+Intersects a ray with an axis-aligned plane defined by an anchor point, extent, and direction index `d`. It returns the intersection distance `t` and barycentric-like coordinates `u, v`. The method uses a direction index to permute coordinate axes, aligning the plane normal with a single axis to simplify the intersection calculation. It sets itself apart by generalizing to any axis-aligned plane rather than a bounded rectangle, and is chosen when only the plane intersection is needed without 2D extent checks [G].
 
 ### [Precise Rectangle-Ellipse Intersection Test](23336-precise-rectangle-ellipse-intersection-test.md)
-An algorithm to determine if a rectangular tile needs rendering by checking if a projected Gaussian ellipse intersects with it, used to reduce false positives compared to bounding box checks. It improves upon the [Axis-Aligned Rectangle Hit Test](5279-axis-aligned-rectangle-hit-test.md) by performing exact geometric intersection tests rather than conservative bounding volume checks, thereby reducing overdraw in 3D Gaussian Splatting.
+An algorithm to determine if a rectangular tile needs rendering by checking if a projected Gaussian ellipse intersects with it, used to reduce false positives compared to bounding box checks. It improves upon the Axis-Aligned Rectangle Hit Test by performing exact geometric intersection tests rather than conservative bounding volume checks, thereby reducing overdraw in 3D Gaussian Splatting. It sets itself apart by handling elliptical projections instead of flat rectangles, and is chosen when rendering 3D Gaussian splats [G].
 
